{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Pseudocode", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about pseudocode.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations.  Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lecture", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a speech delivered in front of a big audience with academic purposes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, to be honest, I did not pay attention to yesterday's lecture on programming codes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "technology", "type": "name"}, {"content": "applying of science and engineering together in practical uses", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It doesn't matter how much technology advances, even the most sophisticated computer can't get to the level of the human mind.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sophisticated", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an object developed with full of knowledge", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It doesn't matter how much technology advances, even the most sophisticated computer can't get to the level of the human mind.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "simplified", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something  turned into a more basic version of itself", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: True! Programming is frequently using a simplified language.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ambiguity", "type": "name"}, {"content": "that can lead or can be understood in two different senses", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That's the pseudocode, a language that is more natural and readable than any other programming language but it has a solid structure that avoids ambiguity.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "language", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a communicative system of symbols", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You just have to include the basic structure from any programming language.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Search for information about pseudocode. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Identify important aspects of pseudocode in programming. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a brochure to write the main aspects you found. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the brochure with your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I search for information about pseudocode. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify important aspects of pseudcode in programming.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a brochure with pseudocode information. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about pseudocode in programming.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Wh Questions with Auxiliaries in Both Present and past, Be - Do", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When we use <strong>wh-words</strong> for a question, it immediately becomes an open question since the expected  answers are not  anymore  yes or no.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you make <strong>wh-questions</strong>, you put the <strong>wh-Word</strong> first, at the very beginning of the sentence, then you follow the typical question structure:</br> <strong>wh- word</strong> + auxiliary verb + subject +main verb + complement +?</br></br>  Examples:</br> <i><strong>Where do</strong> you use pseudocode?</br> <strong>When did</strong> you learn to write programs in pseudocode?</i></br></br>  Remember that verb to be works as its own auxiliary.</br> <i><strong>Why are</strong> you interested in pseudocode?</i></br></br>  <strong>Wh-questions</strong> can be formed with all tenses following almost the same structure.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What did you do those two hours? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How do you write that kind of code?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbs of Frequency with Present Continuous", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <b>adverbs of frequency</b> to talk about the rate of occurrence in which you do certain activities. Remember that <b>adverbs</b> have different levels of <b>frequency</b>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<b>Adverbs of frequency</b> usually go before the main verb of a sentence. Take a look at the structure:</br></br>Subject + adverb + main verb</br></br>  Example: </br><i>I <b>always</b> remember to use programming codes when designing a web page.</br> He <b>normally</b> uses pseudocode at work</i>.</br></br>An <b>adverb of frequency</b> goes after the verb <b>be</b>. The structure goes like this:</br></br>  Subject + to be + adverb</br></br> Example:</br><i>Most of the programming codes are <b>never</b> like human language.</br> Pseudocode isn't <b>usually</b> complicated.</br></br>The structure with <b>present continuous tense</b> goes like this:</br></br>Subject+ to be + adverb+ verb+ ing+ Complement.</br></br> Example:</br> <i>The company <b>is occasionally thinking</b> in improving the language programming codes when starting the month</i>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Adverb Word</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Frequency Percentage</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Always\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"100%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Frequently\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"90%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Usually\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"80%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Often\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"70%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sometimes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"60%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Occasionaly\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"50%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"