0re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I look up for more information about pseudocode.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n2le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<strong>Luke:</strong> Hi Sam</br>\n<strong>Sam:</strong> Hey Luke, how are you today?</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> In fact, I'm thinking deeply about something.</br>\n<strong>Sam:</strong> And why is that?</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> Well, to be honest, I'm rarely paying attention to lectures these days, so I have no idea about yesterday's one on programming languages.</br>\n<strong>Sam:</strong> So, what did you do those two hours?</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> At 10:00, I am usually sleeping because I feel too tired. </br>\n<strong>Sam:</strong> You're always falling asleep during lectures.</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> I know. Anyway, do you mind telling me how it was?</br>\n<strong>Sam:</strong> Not at all. Well, the lecture was mainly on pseudocode.</br>", "image": "enpe7n2le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "37000", "text": "<strong>Luke:</strong> Pseudocode, what is that?</br>\n<strong>Sam:</strong> As you know, it doesn't matter how much technology advances, even the most sophisticated computer can never get to the level of the human mind. A  proof of it is that programming languages are still very basic if we compare them with human language.</br>\n<strong>Luke:</strong> That's amazing, even though sometimes they can be way too difficult to learn.</br>\n<strong>Sam:</strong> True! Programming is frequently using a simplified language. That's the pseudocode, a language that is more natural and readable than any other programming language, but it has a solid structure that avoids ambiguity.</br>", "image": "enpe7n2le02ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "79000", "text": "<strong>Luke:</strong> How do you write it? Did you take notes of any example?</br>\n<strong>Sam:</strong> Of course! You just have to include the basic structure from any programming language. Then, once you checked  that the  writing  in the pseudocode is correct, you have to recode it in any programming language you want. This pseudocode can determine the way to charge sales tax for an online purchase.</br></br>Getting the customer's state</br>\nIf state is \u201cCS\u201d then</br>\nTax = Price * .075</br>\nTotal = Price + Tax</br>\nEnd If</br></br>If (state == \u201cCS\u201d) {</br>\nTax = Price * .075;</br>\nTotal = Price + Tax;</br></br>\n<b>Luke</b>: Wow! It looks pretty complex!</br>\n<b>Sam</b>: Not at all, think of it as an easier way to program but keeping in mind the inside process!</br>\n<b>Luke</b>: Got it!", "image": "enpe7n2le02ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n2le02ob10re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}